docs: two cache knobs, and which one a "cache for a day" rule is

The browser half is fixed (a Cache Rule now lets `_headers` max-age=0 through; the zone had been rewriting it to 300). The remaining staleness is Edge TTL, which only a Cache Rule sets and which a longer TTL makes worse. Corrects a claim in OPEN.md §2b and `_headers` that is no longer true.
